  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n- Anticipate cooler temperatures and periods of valley rain and\n  mountain snow Saturday evening through Monday morning.\n\nRadar currently shows weak returns northwest of Missoula. Some of\nthese returns may be producing light precipitation, especially in\nthe mountains. Use caution during the morning commute if \ntraveling across Lookout or Marias Passes as slick driving may be \npresent although this is a very low probability outcome. \n\nThe rest of the day trends drier and these conditions will \ncontinue into Friday. Temperatures will remain near normal for \nthis time of year, but physically it might feel cool as cloud \ncover limits the warmth of sunshine, especially on Friday. \n\nThe next system arrives on Saturday, snow levels which begin above\n6000 feet may lower to 4500 feet on Sunday. The majority of\nprecipitation will fall south of I-90 and a trace to 3 slushy\ninches may accumulate at Lost Trail Pass, most elevations of Lemhi\nCounty ID, and higher valleys of southwest MT. Sunday morning at \nLost Trail Pass there may be brief periods of winter driving \nconditions. \n\nHigh pressure is forecast through at least midweek (3-5 Nov) with\ntemperatures returning a few degrees above normal. This time of\nyear high pressure would allow for valley inversions, which could\nkeep valleys from full warming potential along with patchy morning\nfog or low stratus clouds.",
